  "worked_solution": "To solve this problem, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series.\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d)\n$$\n\nSince we know two terms of the arithmetic series, we can find its common difference, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\frac{{a}_{5}-{a}_{1}}{5-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{5-(-3)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{4} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting ${a}_{1}=-3$, $d=2$, and ${S}_{N}=192$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 192 & =\\frac{N}{2}(2(-3)+(N-1)(2)) \\\\ 192 & =\\frac{N}{2}(-6+2N-2) \\\\ 192 & =\\frac{N}{2}(2N-8) \\\\ 192 & =N(N-4) \\\\ 192 & ={N}^{2}-4N \\\\ {N}^{2}-4N-192 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the equation above, the quadratic formula gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N & =\\frac{-(-4)\\pm \\sqrt{(-4)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot (-192)}}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm \\sqrt{784}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm 28}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $N=16$ or $N=-12.$ We disregard the negative solution since $N$ must be positive.\n\nTherefore, our series has $N=16$ terms.",
